<title>USA: NY/NJ Port Auth. taps Citicorp, Lehman for bonds.</title>
<headline>NY/NJ Port Auth. taps Citicorp, Lehman for bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Port Authority of New York and New Jersey, which on Thursday authorized issuing as much as $1.2 billion of special project bonds, said it selected Citicorp and Lehman Brothers to lead the bond syndicate.</p>
<p>A source familiar with the agency's plans said it expected to sell two series of bonds, with the first sale taking place in December.</p>
<p>No further details were immediately available.</p>
<p>&quot;It's really premature for the specific information to be laid out. It's still in the planning stages,&quot; said the source, who declined to be named.</p>
<p>--Joan Gralla, 212-859-1654</p>
